# Cloudflared Named Tunnel — Systemd Service Template

## Purpose
Run Cloudflare Named Tunnel as a persistent systemd service with token-based auth. Auto-starts on boot, restarts on failure.

---

## Service File: `/etc/systemd/system/cloudflared.service`

```ini
[Unit]
Description=Cloudflare Tunnel - hafjet-n8n
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=hafizi145
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/cloudflared tunnel run --token <TUNNEL_TOKEN>
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
KillMode=process

# Security hardening
NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=read-only
ReadWritePaths=/home/hafizi145/.cloudflared

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

---

## Setup Commands

```bash
# 1. Get tunnel token from Cloudflare Dashboard
# Zero Trust → Networks → Tunnels → hafjet-n8n → Copy token

# 2. Create service file (replace <TUNNEL_TOKEN>)
sudo tee /etc/systemd/system/cloudflared.service > /dev/null << 'EOF'
[Unit]
Description=Cloudflare Tunnel - hafjet-n8n
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=hafizi145
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/cloudflared tunnel run --token <TUNNEL_TOKEN>
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
KillMode=process

NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=read-only
ReadWritePaths=/home/hafizi145/.cloudflared

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
EOF

# 3. Reload systemd
sudo systemctl daemon-reload

# 4. Enable & start
sudo systemctl enable cloudflared
sudo systemctl start cloudflared

# 5. Verify
sudo systemctl status cloudflared --no-pager
sudo journalctl -u cloudflared -n 30 --no-pager
```

---

## Verification

```bash
# Check service status
sudo systemctl status cloudflared

# Check logs (look for "Connection established")
sudo journalctl -u cloudflared -f

# Test tunnel
curl -I https://n8n.hafjet.my
curl https://n8n.hafjet.my/healthz
```

---

## Troubleshooting

| Issue | Check | Fix |
|-------|-------|-----|
| Service fails immediately | `journalctl -u cloudflared` | Verify token is correct; check `cloudflared tunnel list` |
| "Cannot determine default origin certificate path" | Logs show cert.pem missing | Use `--token` auth (not `tunnel run hafjet-n8n`) |
| Tunnel inactive in dashboard | `cloudflared` not connecting | Check Split Tunnels: remove `100.64.0.0/10` from Exclude |
| DNS not resolving | `dig n8n.hafjet.my` | Wait for NS propagation; verify nameservers at registrar |

